
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gardening Guides | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  heroTitle="Gardening Guides"
  heroText="Practical gardening knowledge, plant references, and inspiration for beautiful outdoor spaces."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Art of Gardening</p>
    <h1>Gardening Knowledge & Reference Library</h1>
    <p>
      Explore practical gardening guides covering garden planning,
      soil preparation, planting, pruning, plant care, and seasonal
      maintenance. Whether you are creating a new garden or caring
      for an established landscape, discover helpful information
      to guide you through every season.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <a class="card" href="#garden-planning">
      <h3>Garden Planning & Design</h3>
      <p>Garden layouts, design principles, colour schemes, garden rooms, and choosing the right plants.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#soil">
      <h3>Soil & Composting</h3>
      <p>Understanding soil structure, improving fertility, composting, and preparing planting beds.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#planting">
      <h3>Planting & Propagation</h3>
      <p>Planting techniques, seeds, bulbs, divisions, cuttings, and growing new plants.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#plant-care">
      <h3>Plant Care & Maintenance</h3>
      <p>Watering, feeding, mulching, pruning, and maintaining healthy plants.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#trees-shrubs">
      <h3>Trees & Shrubs</h3>
      <p>Choosing, planting, establishing, and maintaining ornamental trees and shrubs.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#flowers">
      <h3>Flowers & Perennials</h3>
      <p>Annuals, perennials, flowering shrubs, bulbs, and creating continuous seasonal colour.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#vegetables">
      <h3>Vegetable & Herb Gardens</h3>
      <p>Growing vegetables, culinary herbs, companion plants, and productive kitchen gardens.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#seasonal">
      <h3>Seasonal Gardening</h3>
      <p>Spring preparation, summer maintenance, autumn planting, and winter protection.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#water">
      <h3>Water & Irrigation</h3>
      <p>Efficient watering, irrigation systems, drainage, and conserving garden moisture.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#pests">
      <h3>Garden Pests & Problems</h3>
      <p>Identifying common garden pests, plant diseases, and practical prevention methods.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#pollinators">
      <h3>Wildlife & Pollinator Gardens</h3>
      <p>Creating welcoming habitats for bees, butterflies, birds, and beneficial insects.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#containers">
      <h3>Container & Small-Space Gardening</h3>
      <p>Planters, pots, raised beds, patios, balconies, and creative small-space planting.</p>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="garden-planning">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 · Design & Preparation</p>
    <h2>Garden Planning & Design</h2>
    <p>
      A successful garden begins with thoughtful planning.
      Consider the size and shape of your space, sunlight,
      soil conditions, drainage, views, and the relationship
      between different garden areas.
    </p>
    <p>
      Establish a clear design direction by selecting a style,
      creating focal points, arranging pathways, and choosing
      plants that complement one another in height, texture,
      form, and seasonal interest.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="soil">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 · Building Healthy Foundations</p>
    <h2>Soil & Composting</h2>
    <p>
      Healthy soil provides the foundation for vigorous plant
      growth. Learn about soil texture, structure, drainage,
      organic matter, and the importance of maintaining
      balanced soil conditions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Compost, leaf mould, and suitable organic amendments
      can improve soil structure and support beneficial
      soil organisms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="planting">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 · Growing New Plants</p>
    <h2>Planting & Propagation</h2>
    <p>
      Discover the fundamentals of planting trees, shrubs,
      perennials, annuals, bulbs, and seeds. Understand
      planting depth, spacing, root preparation, and
      aftercare.
    </p>
    <p>
      Explore propagation techniques including seed sowing,
      division, layering, and stem cuttings to increase
      your collection of garden plants.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="plant-care">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 · Everyday Gardening</p>
    <h2>Plant Care & Maintenance</h2>
    <p>
      Learn how to maintain healthy plants through appropriate
      watering, feeding, mulching, deadheading, pruning,
      and regular observation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Good maintenance practices help plants establish,
      encourage flowering, improve appearance, and reduce
      unnecessary garden problems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="trees-shrubs">
    <p class="eyebrow">05 · Structure & Form</p>
    <h2>Trees & Shrubs</h2>
    <p>
      Trees and shrubs provide structure, privacy, shade,
      shelter, and year-round interest. Explore how to select
      suitable varieties, prepare planting sites, establish
      healthy root systems, and maintain mature specimens.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="flowers">
    <p class="eyebrow">06 · Colour & Seasonal Beauty</p>
    <h2>Flowers & Perennials</h2>
    <p>
      Discover the possibilities of annuals, perennials,
      flowering shrubs, roses, and flowering bulbs.
      Learn to combine plants for harmonious colour,
      varied textures, and a succession of blooms
      throughout the growing season.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="vegetables">
    <p class="eyebrow">07 · Productive Gardens</p>
    <h2>Vegetable & Herb Gardens</h2>
    <p>
      Create a productive kitchen garden with vegetables,
      culinary herbs, and edible flowers. Explore crop
      rotation, succession planting, seed starting,
      harvesting, and practical garden layouts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="seasonal">
    <p class="eyebrow">08 · Gardening Throughout the Year</p>
    <h2>Seasonal Gardening</h2>
    <p>
      Follow the changing needs of your garden through
      spring, summer, autumn, and winter. Discover when
      to prepare beds, plant, prune, divide perennials,
      collect seeds, and protect sensitive plants.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="water">
    <p class="eyebrow">09 · Water Management</p>
    <h2>Water & Irrigation</h2>
    <p>
      Understand the importance of efficient watering,
      suitable irrigation methods, good drainage,
      and moisture retention. Learn how to adapt
      watering practices to plant requirements,
      soil conditions, and seasonal weather.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="pests">
    <p class="eyebrow">10 · Garden Health</p>
    <h2>Garden Pests & Problems</h2>
    <p>
      Learn to recognize common signs of insect damage,
      fungal diseases, nutrient deficiencies, and
      environmental stress. Explore preventative
      gardening practices and integrated approaches
      to managing garden problems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="pollinators">
    <p class="eyebrow">11 · Gardening for Nature</p>
    <h2>Wildlife & Pollinator Gardens</h2>
    <p>
      Encourage biodiversity by choosing nectar-rich
      flowers, providing habitat, and incorporating
      plants that support pollinators and beneficial
      insects. Create a garden that offers food,
      shelter, and seasonal resources for wildlife.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="containers">
    <p class="eyebrow">12 · Creative Gardening</p>
    <h2>Container & Small-Space Gardening</h2>
    <p>
      Make the most of patios, balconies, courtyards,
      and smaller outdoor spaces. Explore container
      selection, suitable growing media, plant
      combinations, and creative arrangements
      for pots and raised beds.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Continue Exploring</p>
    <h2>More Gardening Inspiration</h2>
    <p>
      Visit our Gardening section for additional
      articles, ideas, and inspiration for creating
      beautiful and productive outdoor spaces.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/gardening/">Explore Gardening & Landscape Inspiration →</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/resources/">← Return to Resources</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
